SUMMARY:Rooftop Pollinator Garden Maintenance  (Raleigh)
DESCRIPTION:Now that the school year is almost upon us\, NCWF South Wake Conservationists Chapter is returning the rooftop garden at Southeast Raleigh Elementary School to keep it in shape! It’s time to follow up our earlier summer weedings\, and prepare them for the students’ reurn later this month. \nThe sixteen tall beds fully dedicated to pollinators are in need of some weeding. Between the drought and the resiliance of invasive grasses and other plants\, the pollinator plants have had a rough summer. This is where we need your assistance! Can you help? This rooftop garden is a very popular and meaningful program to the students and administration. Just bring your personal water bottle and a pair of gardening gloves\, and we’ll supply the rest. Hope you can join us! \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/rooftop-pollinator-garden-maintenance-raleigh/
CATEGORIES:Featured
END:VEVENT
