SUMMARY:Great Southeast Pollinator Census (Marvin)
DESCRIPTION:The Great Southeast Pollinator Census is the perfect Community Science event. This is great for almost all ages\, and no experience is required. As long as you can count\, the rest is easy. Join NCWF Habitat Builders of West Union Chapter and learn about pollinator plants and how to identify our most common pollinators. We provide the data sheets. Participate in the census with us and then do more counts at home! More is always better when it comes to pollinators—more info about the count here https://gsepc.org/.\nDrop-in anytime between 1 PM and 3 PM or stay the whole time!  \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/great-southeast-pollinator-census-marvin-2/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/HBGSEPC-1.png
END:VEVENT
